{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014KeaJZATXdVEqDrnAT6in9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE result\n2\t\n3\tstatus: PASSED\n4\tnode_prompt: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/prompts/N31_repair_acceptance.prompt.v2.md\n5\tpredecessor: N30_UNIT_GRAPH (compact state supplied by the controller, status PASSED)\n6\tgeneration: 1\n7\t\n8\t## What this node built\n9\t\n10\tTwo new top-level modules, per `contracts/node_ownership.v1.md` (\"N31 owns\n11\trepair/acceptance modules, not terminal.py\"):\n12\t\n13\t- `runtime/langgraph_factory/repair.py` — D17 (finding classification), D18\n14\t  (targeted repair planning), D19 (deterministic-vs-model routing), D20\n15\t  (boundary-checked admission), D21 (retest dispatch).\n16\t- `runtime/langgraph_factory/acceptance.py` — D16 (unit denominator\n17\t  reduction), D22 (recompute-and-accept), D23 (checkpoint correlation +\n18\t  cursor advance), plus `prove_exact_manifest_coverage()`, the D24 coverage\n19\t  predicate N32 will call.\n20\t\n21\tNeither module is registered into the compiled graph yet. `routing.py`'s\n22\tguard tables for D16-D23 already exist (built by N20) and this generation's\n23\tfunctions emit exactly the guard values those tables declare\n24\t(`unit_denominator_passed`/`unit_findings_repairable`,\n25\t`partition_complete`/`convergence_exhausted`, `repair_planned`,\n26\t`model_repair`/`deterministic_repair`, `repair_admitted`,\n27\t`retest_frontier_incomplete`/`retest_frontier_complete`, `unit_accepted`,\n28\t`checkpoint_correlated`) — but `add_node`/`add_conditional_edges` wiring\n29\tthese into `graph.py`'s `StateGraph` is N32's write\n30\t(`implementation.graph.v3.yaml`: N32 owns `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py`,\n31\tN31 does not). Every function here is therefore a plain, narrowly-scoped\n32\t`(state, runtime_context) -> update` callable in the same shape N23's\n33\t`model_nodes.py` already uses for D90/D91 — not wrapped in\n34\t`nodes.deterministic_node()`, since that decorator requires a\n35\t`NODE_CATALOGUE` row this generation is not permitted to add (`nodes/__init__.py`\n36\tis not in N31's write set). A future node binds these to catalogue rows\n37\twithout changing this module's bodies.\n38\t\n39\t`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` calls every function\n40\tdirectly against hand-built `FactoryState` fixtures, merged step-to-step\n41\tthrough the real field reducers (`state.FIELD_REDUCERS`), not a mock merge.\n42\t\n43\t## Owner / retest map\n44\t\n45\t| Owner | Channel | Repair route (this generation) | First retest node |\n46\t|---|---|---|---|\n47\t| source interpretation | domain | model (M06) | `D07_CORRELATE_AND_ADMIT_SOURCES` |\n48\t| curriculum domain | domain | model (M06) | `D08_VALIDATE_DOMAIN` |\n49\t| unit content | content | model (M06) | `D09_VALIDATE_CONTENT` |\n50\t| unit visual | visuals | model (M06) unless every named key is an authoritative/library brief, then deterministic | `D10_COMPILE_VISUAL_BRIEFS` |\n51\t| unit layout | layout | deterministic (boundary-scoped pointer correction) | `D13_RENDER_UNIT` |\n52\t\n53\t`repair.RETEST_ORDER_BY_OWNER` carries each owner's full fixed chain (spec\n54\tsection 12's table); D21 dispatches only the first node of that chain — the\n55\tremaining steps are the already-wired unit-path edges (N30) that node's own\n56\tsuccess guard reaches on its own, so D21 is never re-entered for the same\n57\trepair admission.\n58\t\n59\tFrozen limits, enforced exactly where spec section 6.2 assigns them: D17\n60\towns the repeated-fingerprint bound (`MAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS = 2`); D18 owns\n61\tthe numeric attempt bound (`MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN = 3`). An earlier\n62\tdraft of this generation checked both bounds in D17, which made\n63\t`test_attempt_bound_exhausts_before_a_fourth_repair_child` fail (D17 was\n64\texhausting a case the prompt's own TEST item expects D18 to exhaust) — fixed\n65\tby removing the attempt-bound check from D17, per spec's own row split (\"D17\n66\t... repeated bound = exhaustion\" vs. \"D18 ... attempt bound = exhaustion\").\n67\t\n68\t## Denominator trace (D16 / D22, `acceptance.compute_unit_denominator`)\n69\t\n70\tRecomputed identically by D16 (before repair) and D22 (immediately before\n71\tminting an accepted receipt) off whatever heads are *current* at call time.\n72\tCategories enforced this generation: source admission (sha256-resolved),\n73\tdomain check set (`DOMAIN_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), content\n74\tcheck set (`CONTENT_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), visual join\n75\tresult, page inventory + inspection set (exact page count, all PASS), one\n76\tindependent unit review with every blocking finding's `category` mapped\n77\tthrough the code-owned `owner_for_review_category()` table (never trusted\n78\tverbatim from the model), and repair-request closure (no request left\n79\tunresolved). `test_removing_or_failing_any_single_member_makes_d22_reject`\n80\tindependently removes/fails each of the five owner-bearing categories and\n81\tconfirms D22 raises every time; `test_staling_the_content_head_makes_d22_reject`\n82\tconfirms a check recorded against a superseded head is invisible to the\n83\treduction (stale evidence cannot pass) without needing to delete anything —\n84\t`compute_unit_denominator` only counts a check whose `head_hash` equals the\n85\t*current* head.\n86\t\n87\tDocumented, not silently assumed, scope limit: this generation's denominator\n88\ttreats the append-only evidence/log layer and the LangGraph checkpoint layer\n89\tas structurally present (state reducers already enforce their shape) rather\n90\tthan independently re-auditing their hash chain from inside D22 (spec\n91\tsection 13.1 items 13-14). `acceptance.py`'s module docstring records this so\n92\ta future generation tightens it rather than rediscovering the gap.\n93\t\n94\t## Real-D98 traces (TEST 9)\n95\t\n96\t`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` imports\n97\t`runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.terminal` unmodified and calls\n98\t`terminal.write_terminal()` directly — the identical function N22 wrote and\n99\tN32 will call for its two product-terminal sites — never a stand-in:\n100\t\n101\t- `test_a_unit_accepted_candidate_traverses_the_real_d98_and_is_accepted`:\n102\t  a `UNIT_ACCEPTED` candidate built from this generation's real D22/D23\n103\t  output is independently re-derived and accepted by D98's own\n104\t  `_validate_unit_accepted`.\n105\t- `test_a_tampered_unit_accepted_candidate_is_rejected_by_the_real_d98`: the\n106\t  same candidate with a forged `receipt_hash` is rejected and D98 writes\n107\t  `SYSTEM_FAILURE` in its place — no N31 code decided that; D98's own\n108\t  re-derivation did.\n109\t- `test_a_convergence_exhausted_candidate_from_d17_traverses_the_real_d98`:\n110\t  the `terminal_candidate` D18 proposes on attempt-bound exhaustion is\n111\t  independently accepted by D98's `_validate_exhausted`.\n112\t\n113\tNo test in this file, and no code in `repair.py`/`acceptance.py`, writes to\n114\t`nodes/terminal.py`; `terminal.write_terminal.__module__` is asserted to\n115\tstill be `runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.terminal`.\n116\t\n117\t## Commands and results\n118\t\n119\t```\n120\t/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py -v\n121\t=> 32 passed in 0.08s\n122\t(results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/focused_test_run.txt)\n123\t\n124\t/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/ -k plan26 -q\n125\t=> 916 passed, 1 skipped, 175 deselected, 345 subtests passed, 4 failed\n126\t(results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/full_plan26_suite.txt)\n127\t```\n128\t\n129\tThe 4 failures are all in `test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py`\n130\t(`test_mechanical_revalidation_*`, `test_passed_nodes_remain_admissible_and_n31_is_the_sole_frontier_after_harness_change`)\n131\tand are pre-existing environment state, not a regression this