{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Du7ffssKa7pqFq6UbqWGyx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# N30_UNIT_GRAPH result\n2\t\n3\tstatus: PASSED\n4\tgraph_digest: ca4835f71750f93880a965a9879e508641b5f9360b82cb5cc8bdec8d57564f30\n5\tnode_prompt: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/prompts/N30_unit_graph.prompt.v1.md (f78e98cb44f95a2aa108e87301d3e5fcddd0924e68a47333181bf5ebcd7f5e3e)\n6\tgeneration: 10\n7\t\n8\t## Generation 10 — P-N30-001 (ownership correction, closing N90 finding F1)\n9\t\n10\t`P-N30-001` is an approved immutable patch overlay, applied this generation.\n11\tRoot cause chain: N90's finding F1 observed that no real run could ever reach\n12\t`D22_ACCEPT_UNIT`/`UNIT_ACCEPTED`, because `D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE` (this\n13\tnode's own declared handoff row) had no node body anywhere in the tree.\n14\t`P-N31-001` (a separate approved immutable patch, closing that finding) has\n15\tN31 wire D16-D23/M06 into the one production compiled graph by widening the\n16\t`available` sequence `unit_graph.register_unit_path` receives — a change to\n17\t`graph.py`'s call site, not to `unit_graph.py`'s own logic\n18\t(`register_unit_path`, `branch_destinations`, `deferred_destinations`,\n19\t`DEFERRED_EDGES`, `UNIT_BRANCHES`), all of which resolve correctly for\n20\twhatever `available` they are given, unchanged this generation. That widening\n21\thas not merged into this attempt's `graph.py` yet (per P-N30-001's own\n22\tordering note, confirmed below: `graph.py`'s hash is unchanged and\n23\t`binding_inventory()` is still the narrow, pre-correction view), but six of\n24\tthis node's own tests in `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` hardcoded assumptions\n25\tthat hold only *before* that widening, and would fail the moment it lands —\n26\ta structural, unavoidable consequence of the correction, not a defect in\n27\t`unit_graph.py`. Fixed here, all in the one file already in this node's write\n28\tset:\n29\t\n30\t1. `test_the_compiled_graph_registers_every_declared_unit_branch` — already\n31\t   computed `expected = branch_destinations(source, graph_nodes)` from\n32\t   `graph_nodes = set(compiled.get_graph().nodes)` (the real compiled graph's\n33\t   own node set), not from `binding_inventory()`'s deliberately narrow return\n34\t   value, so no change was needed here; confirmed and documented as already\n35\t   correct-by-construction.\n36\t2. `test_a_fresh_episode_executes_the_bootstrap_spine_once_through_langgraph`\n37\t   — asserted `state[\"selected_unit_id\"] == \"U001\"` off the run's final\n38\t   merged state. `selected_unit_id` uses the `replace_current` reducer\n39\t   (`state.py:121`), and once D16-D23 wire, this clean single-unit episode\n40\t   legitimately loops back to a second `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` call whose\n41\t   `manifest_exhausted` guard correctly overwrites it to `None` — a real\n42\t   second call, not a repeat of the first. Fixed to assert `\"U001\"` off\n43\t   `D05`'s own *first* `updates` entry instead, and to assert the final\n44\t   `selected_unit_id` conditionally on whether `D05` ran once or twice.\n45\t3. `test_a_visual_denominator_permutation_produces_an_identical_admitted_head`,\n46\t   `test_the_committed_path_stops_at_a_declared_deferred_edge`, and\n47\t   `test_this_nodes_renderers_are_a_test_double_and_not_exposed_to_n13s_store_gap`\n48\t   — each hardcoded `result[\"deferred_frontier\"] == \"D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE\"`.\n49\t   Fixed to assert, via a new shared helper `_assert_frontier_is_a_declared_row`,\n50\t   only that the frontier `_run_episode` actually observed (the real\n51\t   `KeyError` LangGraph raised, not a re-derived prediction) is *some* row of\n52\t   `DEFERRED_EDGES` — never `None`, never fabricated — without naming which\n53\t   row. (An initial attempt tried re-deriving the expected destination from\n54\t   `trace[-1]`; this does not work for `M05`, whose own update is swallowed\n55\t   by the aborted superstep before it reaches the stream — see item 5 below —\n56\t   so the derivation was corrected to check the observed value's validity\n57\t   rather than independently re-predict it.) The permutation test additionally\n58\t   now asserts `forward[\"deferred_frontier\"] == reverse[\"deferred_frontier\"]`,\n59\t   a real cross-check that visual order cannot change which row the episode\n60\t   halts on.\n61\t4. `test_the_committed_path_stops_at_a_declared_deferred_edge`'s docstring is\n62\t   reworded from \"the episode's real frontier is this node's own GOAL\n63\t   boundary\" (specific to the M05->D16 edge) to \"never a fabricated one\"\n64\t   (general to whichever row is currently open), since its real, durable\n65\t   purpose was always the latter.\n66\t5. `test_the_unobservable_boundary_is_excluded_for_a_stated_reason` is\n67\t   **deliberately left with its hardcoded `\"D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE\"`\n68\t   literal**, per P-N30-001's own escape hatch for a test \"whose entire\n69\t   point was to prove the run stops exactly at the M05->D16 edge.\" Its\n70\t   premise is not just today's specific frontier value — it is that M05 is\n71\t   *unobservable* because the one edge that is currently deferred happens to\n72\t   be M05's own next hop. Once N31 wires D16, that premise inverts: M05's\n73\t   own update becomes observable (the superstep no longer aborts) and M05\n74\t   belongs in `REACHABLE_BOUNDARIES`/the crash matrix instead of being\n75\t   excluded from it. No dynamic re-derivation preserves that meaning — a\n76\t   version that instead asserted \"the frontier is a declared row\" would\n77\t   silently keep passing for the wrong reason once M05 stops being the\n78\t   unobservable node, masking exactly the regression the test exists to\n79\t   catch. This test is therefore expected to start failing, correctly, the\n80\t   moment D16 is wired, and rewriting or retiring it then is N31's (or\n81\t   whichever generation wires D16) to do — recorded in-line in the test's own\n82\t   docstring and here, not routed around with an artificial fixture.\n83\t\n84\tVerification: `tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py` is 93/93 green today,\n85\tunchanged in count from generation 9 (`evidence/N30_UNIT_GRAPH/venv_unit_graph.txt`,\n86\tregenerated). `unit_graph.py` and `graph.py` are untouched (hashes below\n87\tunchanged from generation 9); the patch's own instruction not to touch either\n88\tfile, `repair.py`, or `acceptance.py` is honored. `binding_inventory()` in\n89\tthis attempt's `graph.py` is confirmed still the narrow pre-correction view\n90\t(unchanged hash, and `graph.py:278-309`'s own docstring still documents D16-D23\n91\tand D24-D32 as deliberately absent), consistent with P-N30-001's ordering note\n92\tthat P-N31-001's widening has not merged into this attempt.\n93\t\n94\tOne pre-existing, out-of-scope-by-ownership item surfaced while re-running the\n95\tfull sweep this generation: `tests/runtime/test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py::\n96\ttest_passed_nodes_remain_admissible_after_harness_or_predecessor_change` now\n97\tfails, reporting `N30_UNIT_GRAPH has a PASSED receipt but is inadmissible`\n98\t(`evidence/N30_UNIT_GRAPH/controller_receipt_admissibility_note.txt`). This is\n99\tthe harness's own receipt store observing that this generation's test-file\n100\tedit changed `test_plan26_unit_graph.py`'s hash out from under the still-stale\n101\tgeneration-9 receipt it holds for this node — exactly the kind of\n102\tharness-level pre-condition generation 9's own report already documented as\n103\toutside this node's write set (that file is owned by the harness controller,\n104\tnot by any `implementation.graph.v3.yaml` node, and is excluded by the same\n105\t`--deselect` used there). A fresh receipt for this node resolves it once this\n106\tresult is accepted; it is not evidence of a defect in `unit_graph.py`,\n107\t`graph.py`, or the test file's own assertions, all of which are green on\n108\ttheir own.\n109\t\n110\t`graph_digest` is the sha256 of `im